## fix4 Solution

### Core idea: Deferred initialization via condition variable

Since the V4L2 hardware decoder only produces frames in PLAYING state, and live HLS prevents preroll from delivering frames in PAUSED state, `Init()` must advance the pipeline to PLAYING before it can know the video dimensions. A `std::condition_variable` synchronises the platform thread (running `Init()`) with the GStreamer streaming thread (running `HandoffHandler`).

### Init() flow

```
Init()
  → Preroll()          [set PAUSED, wait up to 5 s for state to settle]
  → set PLAYING        [V4L2 M2M decoder starts producing frames]
  → wait_for(5s, first_frame_ready_)
       |
       |  HandoffHandler (GStreamer streaming thread):
       |    update width/height/pixels inside mutex_buffer_
       |    first_frame_ready_.exchange(true) → notify_all()
       |    initialized_.exchange(true) → OnNotifyInitialized() [if Init timed out]
       |
  → first_frame_ready_.load() && !initialized_.exchange(true)
  → OnNotifyInitialized() + OnNotifyPlaying(true)   [platform thread, normal case]
```

### Key design decisions

| Decision | Rationale |
|----------|-----------|
| `sync=TRUE, qos=FALSE` on fakesink | Clock-paced video = A/V sync. `qos=FALSE` suppresses quality-of-service frame drops. |
| No `async=FALSE` on fakesink | `async=TRUE` (default) means fakesink participates in preroll and the pipeline won't report PAUSED-complete until fakesink is ready — this is what we want. |
| `initialized_` is `std::atomic<bool>` | Guards `OnNotifyInitialized()` from being called twice in the race between Init() (platform thread) and HandoffHandler (streaming thread). `exchange(true)` returns the old value; only the first caller (old value = false) calls OnNotifyInitialized(). |
| `first_frame_ready_` is separate from `initialized_` | Lets Init() distinguish "frame arrived, I should do init" from "frame didn't arrive in 5s, HandoffHandler will do init later" without needing an extra lock. |
| width/height/pixels updated inside `mutex_buffer_` in HandoffHandler | `GetFrameBuffer()` holds a shared lock on `mutex_buffer_` — write lock in HandoffHandler ensures no torn read of the pixel buffer pointer. |
| `Preroll()` uses `gst_element_get_state(5s)` not bus poll loop | Simpler; `GST_STATE_CHANGE_NO_PREROLL` from live source is not an error. Bus poll loop required `GST_BUS_PASS` which conflicted with the sync handler. |
| `HandleGstMessage` returns `GST_BUS_DROP` | Sync handler — messages are consumed here and do not need to reach the async bus queue. |
| Buffer: 5 MB / 8 s | Large enough for ≥6 HLS segments at 1.5 Mbps; absorbs segment fetch jitter without stalling. |

