## Pipeline Architecture (fix4)

```
playbin (uri=..., flags=VIDEO|AUDIO|NATIVE_VIDEO|BUFFERING, buffer-size=5MB, buffer-duration=8s)
  |
  +-- video-sink = output (GstBin)
  |     queue → v4l2convert → [video/x-raw,format=RGBA] → fakesink(sync=TRUE,qos=FALSE)
  |                                                          ↑ HandoffHandler
  |
  +-- audio-sink = audio_bin (GstBin)
        audioconvert → audioresample → alsasink(device=PickAudioDevice())
```

### Element rank overrides (applied in CreatePipeline)

| Element | Action | Reason |
|---------|--------|--------|
| `curlhttpsrc` | `GST_RANK_PRIMARY + 300` | Handles HTTPS/TLS correctly; `souphttpsrc` had SSL failures |
| `souphttpsrc` | `GST_RANK_NONE` | Disabled to prevent selection |
| `v4l2h264dec` | `GST_RANK_PRIMARY + 300` | Hardware H.264 decode (V4L2 M2M); software decode was too slow on Pi |

### Changes from upstream Sony that are preserved

1. **`curlhttpsrc` boost / `souphttpsrc` disabled** — HTTPS HLS streams
2. **`v4l2h264dec` rank boost** — hardware H.264 decode
3. **Explicit `alsasink` audio bin** — Buildroot does not include `autoaudiosink`
4. **HDMI auto-detection** (`PickAudioDevice`) — reads `/sys/class/drm/card*-HDMI-A-N/status`, maps to ALSA card via `/proc/asound/cardN/id`; falls back to `plughw:0,0` (3.5mm jack)
5. **HTTP auth headers** — applied via `source-setup` signal on `curlhttpsrc` using `extra-headers` GstStructure

